WordPress/Elementor HTML block with an <iframe> to display an already running application inside your website.

To add your Chronic Kidney Disease Prediction Flask app, the workflow is:

1. Your CKD Flask app must be running online
Your Flask CKD App
       ↓
Deploy to Cloud
       ↓
Get Public URL
       ↓
Example:
https://your-ckd-app.run.app

Important: http://127.0.0.1:8080 will not work inside your public WordPress website because it only runs on your local computer.

2. Add the CKD app URL in Elementor

In the HTML Code section shown in your screenshot, add:

<iframe 
    src="YOUR_CKD_APP_PUBLIC_URL"
    width="100%"
    height="800px"
    style="border: none;">
</iframe>

For example, after deployment:

<iframe 
    src="https://your-ckd-app.run.app"
    width="100%"
    height="800px"
    style="border: none;">
</iframe>

